From: lmoresi <louis.moresi@anu.edu.au>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 18:15:32 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Review: a missing cell inside a ladder assembly is
 refused by its hole, exactly; the area check is a backstop

An area tolerance could separate the wall's excess from a missing 1e-6 sliver
by only about a factor of two each way. A ladder assembly's outlines have no
holes, so its mesh must have V - E + F equal to its number of pieces; a cell
missing from inside, of any size, opens a hole and fails that with no
tolerance (every assembly measured has 1). With the check that no edge
borders more than two triangles (a doubled cell), the area comparison is a
backstop for a missing cell along the boundary, at the perimeter times 1e-8
of the diameter (the wall's excess is 1.7e-10 against 1.0e-9).

test_0906: the missing sliver is now refused by the hole; a missing interior
triangle touching the boundary at one vertex is refused; the doubled-cell and
wall-excess cases stand.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
